The potential of augmented reality to superimpose digital data on the real environment is enormous for indoor navigation. This endeavor explores the creation of an augmented reality (AR) interior navigation system that immerses users in their environment and offers context-aware information and real-time advice. By harnessing AR's potential, this project envisions a future where navigating intricate indoor spaces becomes not only efficient but also engaging, promising to enhance the overall experience for users in various indoor settings. This report explores the technological intricacies, design considerations, and user experience aspects essential for the successful implementation of Indoor Navigation using AR.
II. PROBLEM DEFINITION
The problem addressed in this indoor navigation augmented reality (AR) project is the challenge of efficiently and accurately guiding individuals within complex and often unfamiliar indoor environments. Current navigation systems primarily rely on GPS, which is ineffective indoors, leading to disorientation and inefficiency for users. The project seeks to develop a solution that leverages AR technology to provide real-time, context-aware guidance and location-based information to users, ensuring seamless indoor navigation. By doing so, the goal is to enhance user experiences, increase productivity, and improve accessibility in settings such as shopping malls, airports, hospitals, and large office complexes, ultimately revolutionizing how people navigate and interact with indoor spaces.
