B. Implementation Methodology

LiDAR Data Acquisition:

LiDAR Data Acquisition is used to capture precise 3D spatial information essential for creating detailed and accurate maps or models of physical environments. LiDAR (Light Detection and Ranging) is a technique that employs laser pulses to measure distance and generate comprehensive 3D maps. In indoor navigation, LiDAR enables precise mapping of indoor spaces, real-time object detection, accurate localization, integration with augmented reality, and accessibility solutions for enhanced user experience, safety, and guidance. The project makes use of LiDAR sensors to capture the college premises and convert it into a 3D model.

