Point Cloud Processing serves as a critical stage in refining and optimizing the data obtained from LiDAR technology. By identifying and extracting crucial features, such as walls, doors, and obstacles, the AR-based navigation system is equipped to generate optimized routes, providing efficient and accurate guidance to users. Point clouds generated by LiDAR sensors provide a dense set of 3D coordinates representing the surfaces and objects in an indoor environment. By processing these point clouds, indoor maps can be created with high accuracy. Furthermore, these maps can be used for localization purposes. By comparing real-time LiDAR data with the pre-existing point cloud map, indoor navigation systems can accurately determine a user's location within a building. This precise localization is essential for guiding users along the correct paths. The project utilizes Point Cloud Processing technique to navigate the user from a source site to a destination location using the AR technology and 3D maps generated by LiDAR sensor.

